com/bb_api.h: fix BB_SET_POWER_AUTO's input struct to the real 3 bytes

bb_set_pwr_auto_in_t was a typedef of bb_get_pwr_auto_out_t -- a single
pwr_auto byte -- so ioctl_tab.c sent BB_SET_POWER_AUTO with a 1-byte
payload. The chip takes 3: stock ar_ldy_gnd's own statically linked
client library has { BB_SET_POWER_AUTO, 3, 0 } in its ioctl table, and
both stock streamers fill all 3 bytes (Ghidra):

  ar_ldy_gnd   do_bb_set_auto_power(mode, min, max) -> {mode, max, min}
               mode 0 {0, min+3, min}  power adaptation off
               mode 1 {1, max, min}    adaptation on within [min, max]
               mode 2 {2, dbm, dbm}    "SET disconnect power"
  ar_ldyhs_sky fpv_bb_set_local_power() -> {2, dbm, dbm} before every
               BB_SET_POWER

With the old size the library silently dropped max/min, so nothing
built on this SDK could set the bounds or the disconnected power at all
-- confirmed on hardware that BB_SET_POWER alone moves the value
BB_GET_CUR_POWER reports without changing what the peer receives.
Also defines BB_HAVE_PWR_AUTO_BOUNDS so host code can tell the fixed
struct apart at compile time. Needed by ar8030-lifecycled's persisted output-power setting. Only the
host-side struct size changes; ar8030d forwards the payload as-is.

diff --git a/com/bb_api.h b/com/bb_api.h
--- a/com/bb_api.h
+++ b/com/bb_api.h
@@ -1604,7 +1604,31 @@
 typedef bb_get_cur_pwr_out_t bb_set_pwr_in_t;                   /**<@note 复用获取当前功率输出结构, power取值范围[0-31dbm]*/
 
 /**定义设置命令BB_SET_POWER_AUTO的输入参数结构*/
-typedef bb_get_pwr_auto_out_t bb_set_pwr_auto_in_t;             /**<@note 复用获取功率自适应使能输出结构*/
+/* Fixed on real hardware (2026-09): the chip takes 3 bytes here, not the
+ * single pwr_auto byte this used to be a typedef of -- the vendor's own
+ * statically linked client library (stock ar_ldy_gnd's ioctl table) sends
+ * 3, and both stock streamers fill all 3. With the old 1-byte size this
+ * library silently dropped max/min, so the chip saw garbage/zero bounds.
+ * pwr_auto = mode (decoded from ar_ldy_gnd / ar_ldyhs_sky):
+ *   BB_PWR_AUTO_OFF (0)        power adaptation off
+ *   BB_PWR_AUTO_ON (1)         adaptation on, bounded by [min, max] dBm
+ *   BB_PWR_AUTO_DISCONNECT (2) max/min = transmit power while no link is
+ *                              up (stock always passes max == min) */
+typedef enum {
+    BB_PWR_AUTO_OFF = 0,
+    BB_PWR_AUTO_ON,
+    BB_PWR_AUTO_DISCONNECT,
+} bb_pwr_auto_mode_e;
+
+typedef struct {
+    uint8_t         pwr_auto;                                   /**<@note mode, type: bb_pwr_auto_mode_e (kept this name: SDK apps set .pwr_auto)*/
+    uint8_t         max;                                        /**<@note upper bound, dBm*/
+    uint8_t         min;                                        /**<@note lower bound, dBm*/
+} bb_set_pwr_auto_in_t;
+
+/* Lets host code tell this fixed struct apart from the old 1-byte one at
+ * compile time (ar8030-lifecycled only enables power control with it). */
+#define BB_HAVE_PWR_AUTO_BOUNDS 1
 
 /**定义设置命令BB_SET_FREQ的输入参数结构*/
 typedef struct {
